I finally arrived in Potsdam.
I got out of the S-Bahn.
Then I walked directly into the town.
The weather has become so wonderfully warm today.
Many people also went outside.
Locals and visitors strolled through the streets together.
Everyone enjoyed the bright spring sunshine.
I walked past small shops and cafés.
While doing so, I admired the beautiful old houses.
A street musician played in a big square.
A few small children ran happily around him.
I stopped for a moment and listened to the music.
Then I walked on slowly.
The warm air felt so good.
I immediately got into a really good mood.
This Sunday excursion started perfectly!
